<%# The flash close control. One definition for both branches, because the only thing that differs
    between them is the tint, and the two hand-rolled panels above are already as much duplication as
    this file should carry.

    **No `text-*` colour.** The glyph inherits the banner's ink - green-900 or red-900 - per
    design.md: an icon in an alert or banner takes the container's text colour rather than setting its
    own, which keeps it at the same ratio as the copy beside it. The modal and navbar closes both set
    `text-slate-600`, correctly, because they sit on white; on a tint that would be a new unmeasured
    pair.

    44px, matching the modal close and the drawer close: this is a bare icon control with no other
    affordance, which is the one case where the app uses that figure rather than the 32px a labelled
    ghost button gets.

    `-my-3` keeps it from making the banner taller. The 44px box would otherwise set the row height
    against a 22px line and add 22px to every flash; pulled in by 12px top and bottom it contributes
    20px, which the icon's 20px plus its mt-0.5 already exceeds. Measured: the banner is **56px with
    the button and 56px without it**.

    The hover fill still paints entirely inside the panel, which is the condition attached to every
    negative-margin target in this app - measured at 5px clear of the border at the top and 7px at the
    bottom, and 17px from the right, that being p-4 plus the hairline. %>
<% tones = {
     notice: { hover: "hover:bg-green-100", outline: "focus-visible:outline-green-700" },
     alert: { hover: "hover:bg-red-100", outline: "focus-visible:outline-red-700" }
   } %>
<% t = tones.fetch(tone.to_sym) %>

<button type="button"
        data-action="dismiss#now"
        class="-my-3 ml-auto flex min-h-11 min-w-11 shrink-0 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-lg transition-colors <%= t[:hover] %> focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 <%= t[:outline] %>">
  <span class="sr-only">Dismiss</span>
  <%= lucide_icon "x", class: "size-5 shrink-0" %>
</button>
